<title>USA: Homestake sees Ruby Hill production by Q4.</title>
<headline>Homestake sees Ruby Hill production by Q4.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Homestake Mining Co on Thursday said it expects gold production to begin at its Ruby Hill mine in Nevada in 1997's fourth quarter with forecasts calling for between 105,000 and 110,000 ounces of gold a year.</p>
<p>The estimated cash cost of mining the gold is $140 per ounce and the total cost is $258 per ounce.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said it is continuing a deep drilling program at Ruby Hill to extend a higher-grade ore zone discovered last year.</p>
<p>Earlier, Homestake reported a first quarter profit of $0.34 a share versus $0.09 per share one year ago.</p>
</text>
